From 87478c15edf0d37cb6d60dcdf88fc7473f67a722 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:06:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): wake a park when its producer card finishes even
 if its wake_check can't see it [daveey]

MacBook t_01a17ec75ca4f9f6 parked on hub card t_01a18cb13e96c856 with its own probe
`hermes kanban show ... 2>/dev/null | grep done`. show reads only this host's board, so the probe
exited a clean 1 for 18 h after the producer completed.

On every clean "not yet" the wake-check runner now re-checks the producer card the park's awaiting
record names: local refs on this board, remote refs via kanban_wait_check.check_remote (outside any
write txn, at most once per 15 min per (gateway, ref, board); rc 2/3 never wake). done/archived wakes the
card once with wake_probe_stale reason=producer_finished and a kanban-dispatcher comment; review and
blocked never wake (met-set states a tracker re-parks on with --from). A probe that already runs
wait-check on that card is not second-guessed.

The wake_check description now says show/list read only this host's board, names the cross-gateway
wait-check probe, and says to add --from <status> when the card already sits blocked/review/triage.
